---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How DNAthletic handles personal data — hosting, server logs, fonts, and your rights under the GDPR."
>
  <section class="article">
    <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
      <a href="/" class="back-link">
        <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m15 18-6-6 6-6"/></svg>
        Back to homepage
      </a>

      <header class="article-header">
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="article-subtitle">Datenschutzerklärung — how personal data is handled on this website.</p>
      </header>

      <div class="prose">
        <blockquote>
          <strong>Draft template — review before relying on it.</strong> This policy describes the site's current setup (static site, no cookies, no analytics, self-hosted fonts). Verify the details against your actual configuration and, ideally, have it checked before treating it as legally complete.
        </blockquote>

        <h2>1. Controller</h2>
        <p>
          The controller responsible for data processing on this website is:
        </p>
        <p>
          Nikolas Drimmel<br />
          Mozartring 3, 84405 Dorfen, Germany<br />
          Email: <a href="mailto:nikolas@drimmel.de">nikolas@drimmel.de</a>
        </p>
        <p>Further details are available in the <a href="/impressum">Impressum</a>.</p>

        <h2>2. Hosting</h2>
        <p>
          This website is hosted on the infrastructure of <strong>Cloudflare</strong> (Cloudflare, Inc., 101 Townsend St, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA). When you visit the site, Cloudflare automatically processes technical connection data (such as your IP address) as needed to deliver the pages, ensure security, and maintain stability. This processing is based on our legitimate interest in a secure and efficient online presence (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). Data transfers to the USA are covered by the appropriate safeguards (e.g. EU standard contractual clauses).
        </p>

        <h2>3. Access data &amp; server log files</h2>
        <p>
          For technical operation, the hosting provider may record standard access data in server log files, including: the requested page, date and time of the request, the referring page, the browser type and version, the operating system, and a shortened or full IP address. This data is not merged with other data sources and is used only to operate and secure the site (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).
        </p>

        <h2>4. Fonts</h2>
        <p>
          Web fonts and mathematical typesetting assets are <strong>self-hosted</strong> on this site. No connection is made to Google Fonts or other third-party font services, so no font-related data is transmitted to external providers when you load a page.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Cookies, analytics &amp; tracking</h2>
        <p>
          This website does <strong>not</strong> set cookies, and it does <strong>not</strong> use analytics, advertising, or third-party tracking. No usage profiles are created.
        </p>

        <h2>6. RSS feed</h2>
        <p>
          The site offers an <a href="/rss.xml">RSS feed</a>. Retrieving it works like any ordinary page request; the same access-data considerations apply. Subscribing happens entirely in your own feed reader — no registration or personal data is required from us.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Contact by email</h2>
        <p>
          If you contact me by email, the information you provide (including your email address and message) is stored to process your enquiry. This data is not passed on without your consent and is processed on the basis of Art. 6(1)(b) or (f) GDPR.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Under the GDPR you have the right to access (Art. 15), rectification (Art. 16), erasure (Art. 17), restriction of processing (Art. 18), data portability (Art. 20), and to object to processing (Art. 21). To exercise any of these, contact me at the address above.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Right to lodge a complaint</h2>
        <p>
          You have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory authority, in particular in the member state of your residence, workplace, or the place of the alleged infringement.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Data security</h2>
        <p>
          This site is served over an encrypted TLS (HTTPS) connection to protect the transmission of data.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          This policy may be updated to reflect changes to the website or to legal requirements. The current version always applies.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
